From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] restore normal RXDMA layout after monitor filtering

The actual KIWI monitor 1.0 build explicitly sets rxdma1_enable=0. Its monitor
filter update then programs RXDMA_BUF, the normal data ring, using the monitor
layout. Both full and other-BSS-only filter experiments lost 47/48 gateway
responses, including after deleting the monitor until stock restoration.
Under 0009 only and only with the shared-ring setting, reapply the existing
architecture-specific normal RX ring configuration after monitor filter
update/reset. Preserve the separate monitor status-ring configuration.
This verifies whether ordinary receive can resume without dropping the STA
association; it does not claim full monitor data reception, timeslot scheduling
or AWDL coexistence. No new hardware ring or DMA ownership is fabricated.

diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/1.0/dp_mon_filter_1.0.c
@@ -1015,6 +1015,19 @@
 		return QDF_STATUS_E_FAILURE;
 	}
 
+	if (marionette_sta_monitor_enabled() &&
+	    !soc->wlan_cfg_ctx->rxdma1_enable) {
+		/* Monitor config targets RXDMA_BUF on this shared-ring device.
+		 * Reapply the normal architecture-specific RX layout/filters so
+		 * the associated STA never keeps the monitor interpretation.
+		 * The separate monitor status-ring setup above is retained. */
+		if (!soc->arch_ops.dp_rxdma_ring_sel_cfg)
+			return QDF_STATUS_E_NOSUPPORT;
+		status = soc->arch_ops.dp_rxdma_ring_sel_cfg(soc);
+		pr_info("MARIONETTE_STA_NORMAL_RX_RESTORED status=%u monitor=%u\n",
+			status, mon_pdev->monitor_configured);
+	}
+
 	return status;
 }
 
